/**
 * Elfsight floating reviews badge — sitewide.
 *
 * CURRENTLY SET TO DESKTOP ONLY in Elfsight (`badgeVisibilityOnDevices`), so it
 * does not render on mobile at all. On phones the reviews still appear in the
 * full inline section on the homepage and contact page, which is the better
 * presentation anyway — readable cards rather than a pill that must be tapped.
 *
 * Why not just position it on mobile: Elfsight's editor has a mobile/desktop
 * PREVIEW toggle, but it is preview only. The underlying settings are shared,
 * and the widget hardcodes its mobile position regardless:
 *     re ? { position: 'bottom', verticalOffset: 20, horizontalOffset: 0 } : i
 * Position and size edits made against the mobile preview do nothing. Confirmed
 * both in the bundle and by the owner testing it in the dashboard.
 *
 * That left it sitting on top of the sticky call bar, and on a contractor's
 * site the phone call is the conversion, so the badge was switched off there.
 *
 * DO NOT "fix" this with a CSS or JS override. An earlier attempt forced
 * `bottom: <clearance> !important` onto the widget; it did not work, and if it
 * ever did it would silently beat the Elfsight settings, so changing anything in
 * their editor would appear to do nothing. Two facts, both expensive to learn:
 *
 *   - The widget mounts into `attachShadow({ mode: 'open' })`. Shadow DOM
 *     encapsulates styles, so an external stylesheet cannot reach it at all,
 *     no matter how the selector is written. Anything that appears to work from
 *     the outside is acting on a light-DOM wrapper, not the badge.
 *   - Its class names come from styled-components and are build hashes that
 *     change between releases, so they were never a stable hook either.
 *
 * Between those two, every in-code route to moving this badge is either
 * impossible or fragile. The vendor setting is the correct place, and it exists.
 */
